This product's design and some rules/prompts were adapted from:

- Cicada (知了), https://github.com/wquguru/cicada — Apache License 2.0.
  Speech segmentation rules (0.6 s pause, 8 s maximum cut at the quietest frame, 30 ms onset),
  the "never speak untranslated text" rule, interpreter prompt wording and the evidence-linked
  meeting-notes structure.
- Parrots, https://github.com/smitea/parrots — MIT License.
  Clause-level early submission idea and pinyin-based hot-word correction idea.
- HuiYi (会译), https://github.com/LingyiChen-AI/huiyi — Apache License 2.0.
  Glossary applied to recognition, translation and notes; summary templates.
- electron-audio-loopback, https://github.com/alectrocute/electron-audio-loopback — MIT License.

Third-party components used at runtime:

- sherpa-onnx / sherpa-onnx-node (Apache License 2.0), with Silero VAD (MIT), SenseVoice
  (FunASR model license) and Whisper (MIT) models downloaded on first use.
- Microsoft Cognitive Services Speech SDK for JavaScript (MIT).
- pinyin-pro (MIT), zod (MIT), ws (MIT), qrcode (MIT), selfsigned (MIT), React (MIT), Electron (MIT).
- cloudflared (Apache License 2.0), downloaded on demand for public room links.
- BlackHole (GPL-3.0) and VB-CABLE (donationware) are NOT bundled; users install them themselves.
